(function(E){ const x = E["exam-02"] = E["exam-02"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x02-r3"] = {"id":"x02-r3","patterns":["RA-tech","GT3-nature","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"title":{"en":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","tr":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","fa":"Reading ۳: متن ۳ (Passage 3) / بخش ۳ (Section 3)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a writer’s argument: answer multiple-choice questions, complete a summary from a box of words, decide YES, NO or NOT GIVEN about the writer’s views, and choose the best title.","tr":"Bu derste bir yazarın düşünce çizgisini takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayacak, bir özeti kelime kutusundan tamamlayacak, yazarın görüşleri için YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verecek ve en iyi başlığı seçeceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری استدلال یک نویسنده را دنبال کنی: به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای جواب بدهی، یک خلاصه را از کادر کلمه‌ها کامل کنی، درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده بین YES، NO و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بهترین عنوان را انتخاب کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to choose a heading for each section of a long article, complete a short summary with single words, and answer multiple-choice questions about details.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir makalenin her bölümü için bir başlık seçmeyi, kısa bir özeti tek kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve ayrıntılarla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری برای هر بخش یک مقاله‌ی بلند عنوان انتخاب کنی، یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه را با تک‌کلمه‌ها کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی جزئیات جواب بدهی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 3: an argument","tr":"Reading Passage 3: bir görüş yazısı","fa":"Reading Passage 3: یک متن استدلالی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a writer’s argument: answer multiple-choice questions, complete a summary from a box of words, decide YES, NO or NOT GIVEN about the writer’s views, and choose the best title.","tr":"Bu derste bir yazarın düşünce çizgisini takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayacak, bir özeti kelime kutusundan tamamlayacak, yazarın görüşleri için YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verecek ve en iyi başlığı seçeceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری استدلال یک نویسنده را دنبال کنی: به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای جواب بدهی، یک خلاصه را از کادر کلمه‌ها کامل کنی، درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده بین YES، NO و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بهترین عنوان را انتخاب کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Box","tr":"Kutu","fa":"کادر"},"value":"A-I"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: computers and public decisions","tr":"Bu sınav: bilgisayarlar ve kamu kararları","fa":"این آزمون: کامپیوترها و تصمیم‌های عمومی"},"intro":{"en":"Passage 3 is usually the hardest: a long argument, often about technology, society or the mind. The writer takes a position and answers other people’s views, so you must keep track of whose opinion each sentence gives.","tr":"Passage 3 genelde en zorudur: çoğu zaman teknoloji, toplum ya da zihin hakkında uzun bir görüş yazısı. Yazar bir tutum alır ve başkalarının görüşlerine cevap verir; her cümlenin kimin görüşünü verdiğini izlemelisin.","fa":"Passage 3 معمولاً سخت‌ترین است: یک استدلال طولانی، اغلب درباره‌ی فناوری، جامعه یا ذهن. نویسنده موضع می‌گیرد و به نظر دیگران جواب می‌دهد، پس باید حواست باشد هر جمله نظرِ چه کسی را می‌گوید."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An argument about computer decisions","tr":"Bilgisayar kararları üzerine bir tartışma yazısı","fa":"یک استدلال درباره‌ی تصمیم‌گیریِ کامپیوترها"},"asks":{"en":"An opinion article: the writer explains where computer programs help public services, then gives three limits and a solution. The questions test the writer’s views, so separate what the writer thinks from what supporters or researchers say.","tr":"Bir görüş yazısı: yazar bilgisayar programlarının kamu hizmetlerinde nerede işe yaradığını anlatıyor, sonra üç sınır ve bir çözüm sunuyor. Sorular yazarın görüşlerini ölçer; yazarın düşündüğünü destekçilerin ya da araştırmacıların söylediğinden ayır.","fa":"یک مقاله‌ی نظری: نویسنده توضیح می‌دهد برنامه‌های کامپیوتری کجا به خدمات عمومی کمک می‌کنند، بعد سه محدودیت و یک راه‌حل می‌آورد. سؤال‌ها نظر نویسنده را می‌سنجند، پس فکرِ نویسنده را از حرف طرفداران یا پژوهشگران جدا کن."},"fields":["What supporters say","Where programs work","Limit 1: old data","Limit 2: explanation","Limit 3: responsibility","The reply","The solution","Cost"],"words":[{"a":"consistent","b":"treats every case the same way","tr":"tutarlı","fa":"یکنواخت، ثابت‌قدم"},{"a":"underestimate","b":"think something is smaller than it is","tr":"hafife almak","fa":"دست‌کم گرفتن"},{"a":"routine","b":"ordinary and repeated","tr":"rutin","fa":"روزمره و تکراری"},{"a":"neutral","b":"not taking sides / fair","tr":"tarafsız","fa":"بی‌طرف"},{"a":"go unnoticed","b":"nobody sees it","tr":"fark edilmemek","fa":"دیده نشدن"},{"a":"entitled to","b":"has the right to","tr":"hakkı olmak","fa":"حق داشتن"},{"a":"I am not convinced","b":"I doubt it / I disagree","tr":"ikna olmadım","fa":"قانع نشده‌ام"},{"a":"recommendation","b":"advice / what it suggests","tr":"öneri","fa":"توصیه"},{"a":"blindly","b":"without thinking or checking","tr":"körü körüne","fa":"کورکورانه"},{"a":"appeal","b":"ask for a decision to be looked at again","tr":"itiraz etmek","fa":"اعتراض کردن، درخواست بازبینی"},{"a":"adopt","b":"start to use","tr":"benimsemek, kullanmaya başlamak","fa":"به کار گرفتن"},{"a":"plainly","b":"clearly / obviously","tr":"açıkça","fa":"آشکارا"}],"traps":[{"en":"Whose view? \"Supporters argue...\" and \"some researchers argue...\" are other people. The writer’s view comes with I, I believe, I am not convinced.","tr":"Kimin görüşü? \"Destekçiler savunuyor...\" ve \"bazı araştırmacılar savunuyor...\" başka insanlardır. Yazarın görüşü I, I believe, I am not convinced ile gelir.","fa":"نظرِ چه کسی؟ «طرفداران می‌گویند...» و «بعضی پژوهشگران می‌گویند...» دیگران‌اند. نظر نویسنده با I، I believe و I am not convinced می‌آید."},{"en":"YES / NO / NOT GIVEN is about the writer’s opinion, not about facts. If the writer never gives a view on a point, the answer is NOT GIVEN, even if the topic is mentioned.","tr":"YES / NO / NOT GIVEN gerçeklerle değil, yazarın görüşüyle ilgilidir. Yazar bir konuda hiç görüş bildirmiyorsa, konu geçse bile cevap NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"YES / NO / NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی نظر نویسنده است، نه واقعیت‌ها. اگر نویسنده درباره‌ی نکته‌ای هیچ نظری نمی‌دهد، جواب NOT GIVEN است، حتی اگر موضوع اسمش آمده باشد."}],"example":{"text":"\"Some economists claim that the new tax will pay for itself within five years. I find this hard to believe.\"","item":"Statement: The new tax will pay for itself within five years. YES, NO or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"The claim belongs to \"some economists\"; the writer finds it \"hard to believe\", which goes against it.","tr":"İddia \"bazı ekonomistlere\" ait; yazar buna \"inanmakta zorlanıyor\", yani karşı çıkıyor.","fa":"این ادعا مال «بعضی اقتصاددان‌ها»ست؛ نویسنده «باورش برایش سخت است»، یعنی مخالف است."}}},{"id":"RA-tech-debate","ctx":["RA-tech"],"title":{"en":"Debates about new technology","tr":"Yeni teknoloji üzerine tartışmalar","fa":"بحث درباره‌ی فناوری‌های تازه"},"asks":{"en":"A discussion of a new technology: robot referees, artificial intelligence, space travel, cashless payment. The writer weighs benefits against risks; YES/NO/NOT GIVEN and multiple choice test the writer’s conclusion.","tr":"Yeni bir teknolojinin tartışıldığı bir metin: robot hakemler, yapay zekâ, uzay yolculuğu, nakitsiz ödeme. Yazar yararları risklerle tartar; YES/NO/NOT GIVEN ve çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın vardığı sonucu sınar.","fa":"بحثی درباره‌ی یک فناوری تازه: داور رباتیک، هوش مصنوعی، سفر فضایی، پرداخت بدون پول نقد. نویسنده فایده‌ها را با خطرها می‌سنجد؛ YES/NO/NOT GIVEN و چندگزینه‌ای نتیجه‌گیری نویسنده را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["The writer believes the technology will soon replace people. (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","According to the writer, the main risk is...","The writer mentions the 2018 match to show...","Summary: supporters claim the system is more ___ than people."],"words":[{"a":"replace","b":"take over from / do the job of","tr":"yerini almak","fa":"جایگزین شدن"},{"a":"accurate","b":"precise / makes fewer mistakes","tr":"isabetli","fa":"دقیق"},{"a":"risk","b":"danger / threat","tr":"risk","fa":"خطر"},{"a":"inevitable","b":"will certainly happen","tr":"kaçınılmaz","fa":"اجتناب‌ناپذیر"},{"a":"premature","b":"too early","tr":"erken","fa":"زودهنگام"},{"a":"transparency","b":"being open about how it works","tr":"şeffaflık","fa":"شفافیت"},{"a":"trust","b":"confidence in it","tr":"güven","fa":"اعتماد"},{"a":"flawed","b":"has faults / imperfect","tr":"kusurlu","fa":"معیوب"},{"a":"outweigh","b":"be greater than","tr":"ağır basmak","fa":"بیشتر بودن از"},{"a":"human judgement","b":"people deciding","tr":"insan muhakemesi","fa":"قضاوت انسانی"},{"a":"in theory","b":"on paper / in principle","tr":"teoride","fa":"در تئوری"},{"a":"in practice","b":"when it is actually used","tr":"pratikte","fa":"در عمل"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"In theory... in practice\": the writer usually believes what comes after \"in practice\".","tr":"\"Teoride... pratikte\": yazar genelde \"pratikte\"den sonra geleni savunur.","fa":"«در تئوری... در عمل»: نویسنده معمولاً به چیزی باور دارد که بعد از «در عمل» می‌آید."},{"en":"A prediction made by \"supporters\" is not the writer’s own prediction.","tr":"\"Destekçilerin\" yaptığı tahmin yazarın kendi tahmini değildir.","fa":"پیش‌بینیِ «طرفداران» پیش‌بینی خود نویسنده نیست."}],"example":{"text":"In theory, an automated referee never misses a foul. In practice, the systems tested so far have struggled in crowded penalty areas, and players have found it hard to accept decisions they cannot question.","item":"Statement: The writer believes automated referees already work well in every situation.  (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"\"In practice... have struggled\" contradicts \"work well in every situation\".","tr":"\"Pratikte... zorlandılar\", \"her durumda iyi çalışıyor\" ile çelişir.","fa":"«در عمل... به مشکل خوردند» با «در هر موقعیتی خوب کار می‌کنند» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-tech"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Four tasks in fourteen questions","tr":"On dört soruda dört görev","fa":"چهار تمرین در چهارده سؤال"},"body":{"en":"Questions 27-29: multiple choice, A-D. Questions 30-35: a summary with a box of nine words; six are used. Questions 36-39: YES, NO or NOT GIVEN about the writer’s views. Question 40: the best title for the whole passage.","tr":"Soru 27-29: çoktan seçmeli, A-D. Soru 30-35: dokuz kelimelik kutulu bir özet; altısı kullanılır. Soru 36-39: yazarın görüşleri hakkında YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 40: bütün metin için en iyi başlık.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۲۹: چندگزینه‌ای، A تا D. سؤال‌های ۳۰ تا ۳۵: خلاصه‌ای با کادر نُه کلمه‌ای؛ شش تا استفاده می‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۳۶ تا ۳۹: YES، NO یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده. سؤال ۴۰: بهترین عنوان برای کل متن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Track the writer’s voice","tr":"Yazarın sesini izle","fa":"صدای نویسنده را دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Skim the first and last paragraphs to find the writer’s main position.","tr":"Yazarın ana tutumunu bulmak için ilk ve son paragrafları hızlıca oku.","fa":"پاراگراف اول و آخر را سریع بخوان تا موضع اصلی نویسنده را پیدا کنی."},{"en":"Mark every place where someone else speaks (supporters, researchers, critics) and every place the writer answers with I.","tr":"Başka birinin konuştuğu her yeri (destekçiler, araştırmacılar, eleştirmenler) ve yazarın I ile cevap verdiği her yeri işaretle.","fa":"هر جایی که کس دیگری حرف می‌زند (طرفداران، پژوهشگران، منتقدان) و هر جایی که نویسنده با I جواب می‌دهد علامت بزن."},{"en":"For the summary box, decide the word class of each gap first, then choose from the box by meaning.","tr":"Kutulu özette önce her boşluğun kelime türüne karar ver, sonra kutudan anlama göre seç.","fa":"برای خلاصه‌ی کادردار اول نوع کلمه‌ی هر جای خالی را مشخص کن، بعد از کادر بر اساس معنی انتخاب کن."},{"en":"Leave the title question until last: by then you know the whole argument.","tr":"Başlık sorusunu en sona bırak: o zamana kadar bütün düşünce çizgisini bilirsin.","fa":"سؤال عنوان را برای آخر بگذار: تا آن موقع کل استدلال را می‌دانی."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Whose opinion is it?","tr":"Bu kimin görüşü?","fa":"این نظرِ کیست؟"},"body":{"en":"An option or a statement can repeat what supporters or researchers believe. It is YES only if the writer agrees. \"I am not convinced\" or \"I find this hard to believe\" turns their idea into NO.","tr":"Bir seçenek ya da ifade, destekçilerin ya da araştırmacıların inandığı şeyi tekrar edebilir. Yalnızca yazar katılıyorsa YES’tir. \"I am not convinced\" ya da \"I find this hard to believe\" onların fikrini NO yapar.","fa":"یک گزینه یا جمله ممکن است باورِ طرفداران یا پژوهشگران را تکرار کند. فقط وقتی YES است که نویسنده موافق باشد. «I am not convinced» یا «I find this hard to believe» ایده‌ی آن‌ها را NO می‌کند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One YES / NO / NOT GIVEN, step by step","tr":"Bir YES / NO / NOT GIVEN, adım adım","fa":"یک YES / NO / NOT GIVEN، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer?","text":"\"Many teachers believe that homework should be banned in primary schools. I would not go that far, but I do think it should be short.\"","item":"Statement: Homework should be banned in primary schools.","answer":"NO","walk":[{"en":"Find the point: homework in primary schools.","tr":"Konuyu bul: ilkokulda ödev.","fa":"نکته را پیدا کن: تکلیف در دبستان."},{"en":"\"Many teachers believe\" is not the writer. The writer says \"I would not go that far\".","tr":"\"Many teachers believe\" yazar değil. Yazar \"o kadar ileri gitmem\" diyor.","fa":"«Many teachers believe» نظر نویسنده نیست. نویسنده می‌گوید «تا این حد پیش نمی‌روم»."},{"en":"The writer disagrees with a ban: NO.","tr":"Yazar yasağa katılmıyor: NO.","fa":"نویسنده با ممنوعیت مخالف است: NO."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Critics say the scheme is too expensive. Whether it will reduce crime, only time will tell.\" Statement: \"The writer believes the scheme will reduce crime.\" YES, NO or NOT GIVEN?","options":["YES","NOT GIVEN","NO"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Only time will tell\" means the writer gives no view either way.","tr":"\"Zaman gösterecek\", yazarın iki yönde de görüş bildirmediği anlamına gelir.","fa":"«زمان نشان خواهد داد» یعنی نویسنده هیچ نظری، نه موافق نه مخالف، نمی‌دهد."}},"remember":{"en":"Separate the writer’s voice from other voices. YES and NO need the writer’s own view.","tr":"Yazarın sesini diğer seslerden ayır. YES ve NO için yazarın kendi görüşü gerekir.","fa":"صدای نویسنده را از صداهای دیگر جدا کن. YES و NO نظرِ خودِ نویسنده را لازم دارند."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 3","title":{"en":"What the machines cannot decide","tr":"Makinelerin karar veremeyeceği şeyler","fa":"چیزهایی که ماشین‌ها نمی‌توانند تصمیم بگیرند"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-tech"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.","passage":"What the machines cannot decide\n\nAcross the world, public bodies are handing decisions to computer programs. Local councils use them to decide which buildings to inspect, which families may need support from social workers and how to plan bus routes; national governments use them to check tax returns and benefit claims. Supporters of these systems argue that they are cheaper than human staff and, above all, more consistent: a program does not get tired, does not have bad days and treats every case by the same rules. I have some sympathy with this view, and I have seen such systems work well in the right setting. But I believe that the limits of these tools are being seriously underestimated, and that some decisions should never be left to them.\n\nLet me begin with what they do well. Where a task is routine, where the rules are clear and where there is a great deal of reliable data, a well-designed program can be extremely useful. Predicting which bridges are most likely to need repair, using information from sensors fixed to the structures, is one good example. Adjusting the timing of traffic lights to the flow of vehicles is another, and similar programs already help water companies to find leaking pipes. In cases like these, a mistake is usually easy to notice and to correct, and nobody's life is changed by a single wrong prediction.\n\nThe difficulties begin when programs are used to make judgements about people. Most of these systems learn from records of past decisions, and the past is not a neutral teacher. Consider a city that used a program to decide where to send its building inspectors. The program was trained on years of inspection records. Because inspectors had always concentrated on poorer districts, the records showed most problems there, so the program kept sending inspectors back to the same streets, while dangerous conditions in wealthier areas went unnoticed. The machine did not create the unfairness; it made it permanent, and harder to see.\n\nThe second difficulty concerns explanation. In a democracy, a person who is refused a benefit or a licence is entitled to ask why, and to receive an answer they can understand and, if necessary, challenge. Many modern systems cannot provide this. They combine hundreds of factors in ways that even their designers find hard to describe. Some researchers argue that an explanation can be produced afterwards by a second program which describes, in simple terms, what the first one probably did. I am not convinced. An explanation that is constructed after the event is a story about a decision, not the reason for it.\n\nThe third difficulty is responsibility. In theory, these programs only advise, and a human official makes the final decision. In practice, studies of offices that use them have found that staff very rarely challenge the program's recommendation, especially when they are busy or when the recommendation is presented as a score. When things go wrong, it becomes unclear who is responsible: the official who accepted the advice, the department that bought the system, or the company that built it. A decision for which nobody is responsible is a dangerous thing in public life.\n\nIt is often said in reply that human decision-makers are hardly perfect. They are inconsistent, they get tired and they have prejudices of their own. All of this is true, and it would be foolish to pretend that the old ways were fair. But the answer is not to ban these tools, nor to trust them blindly. It is to limit what they are used for. Programs should give advice rather than make final decisions about individuals; the public should be told what data they use; anyone affected should be able to appeal to a person; and every system should be tested regularly for the kind of bias I have described.\n\nNone of this is free, and here lies a final problem. Governments often adopt these systems in order to save money. Yet careful testing, clear explanations and proper human review all cost money too, so the savings may turn out to be smaller than promised. Indeed, several councils have quietly stopped using such systems once the full costs became clear. If a system is only affordable when these protections are removed, that tells us something important about whether it should be used at all.\n\nThe question we should be asking, then, is not whether machines are clever enough to make public decisions. In some narrow areas they plainly are. The question is which decisions belong to people who can be questioned, held responsible and, if they are wrong, asked to think again.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 27-29. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-29 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"In the first paragraph, the writer reports that supporters of these systems value them mainly because they","options":["A are popular with the public.","B cost less and work more consistently.","C can explain their decisions clearly.","D reduce the work of social workers."],"correct":1,"evidence":"they are cheaper than human staff and, above all, more consistent","why":{"en":"\"Cheaper than human staff and, above all, more consistent.\" Social workers are mentioned only as one use.","tr":"\"İnsan personelden daha ucuz ve hepsinden önemlisi daha tutarlı.\" Sosyal hizmet uzmanlarından yalnızca bir kullanım alanı olarak söz ediliyor.","fa":"«ارزان‌تر از کارکنان انسانی و مهم‌تر از همه یکنواخت‌تر». از مددکارها فقط به‌عنوان یک کاربرد اسم برده شده."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"The writer uses the example of the building inspectors to show that","options":["A the inspectors ignored the program’s advice.","B wealthier districts had more dangerous buildings.","C the records had been collected carelessly.","D a program can make an existing unfairness permanent."],"correct":3,"evidence":"it made it permanent, and harder to see","why":{"en":"\"The machine did not create the unfairness; it made it permanent, and harder to see.\"","tr":"\"Makine haksızlığı yaratmadı; onu kalıcı ve görülmesi daha zor hâle getirdi.\"","fa":"«ماشین بی‌عدالتی را نساخت؛ آن را دائمی و دیدنش را سخت‌تر کرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about officials who work with these programs?","options":["A They seldom go against what the program recommends.","B They are trained to question its results.","C They usually prefer their own judgement.","D They are blamed for every mistake."],"correct":0,"evidence":"staff very rarely challenge the program's recommendation","why":{"en":"\"Staff very rarely challenge the program’s recommendation\": seldom go against it.","tr":"\"Personel programın önerisine çok nadiren itiraz ediyor\": ona nadiren karşı çıkıyorlar.","fa":"«کارکنان خیلی به‌ندرت پیشنهاد برنامه را زیر سؤال می‌برند»: به‌ندرت با آن مخالفت می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","PARA-research"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 30-35. Complete the summary using the list of words, A-I, below. Write the correct letter, A-I, in boxes 30-35 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary-box","summaryTitle":"The problems with computer decisions","bank":["A accurate","B challenged","C explanation","D faster","E poorer","F records","G responsible","H smaller","I wealthier"],"questions":[{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"Programs that learn from past ___ may repeat old unfairness.","correct":5,"evidence":"learn from records of past decisions","why":{"en":"\"Most of these systems learn from records of past decisions\": records (F).","tr":"\"Bu sistemlerin çoğu geçmiş kararların kayıtlarından öğrenir\": records (F).","fa":"«بیشتر این سیستم‌ها از سوابقِ تصمیم‌های گذشته یاد می‌گیرند»: records (F)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"In one city, inspectors had always been sent mainly to ___ districts, so problems elsewhere were missed.","correct":4,"evidence":"Because inspectors had always concentrated on poorer districts","why":{"en":"Poorer (E). Wealthier (I) is in the passage too, but those are the areas where problems went unnoticed.","tr":"Poorer (E). Wealthier (I) da metinde geçiyor ama sorunların fark edilmediği bölgeler onlar.","fa":"poorer (E). wealthier (I) هم در متن آمده، اما آن‌ها جاهایی‌اند که مشکل‌ها دیده نشدند."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"A person who is refused a benefit should receive an ___ that they can understand.","correct":2,"evidence":"entitled to ask why, and to receive an answer they can understand","why":{"en":"\"Entitled to ask why, and to receive an answer they can understand\": an explanation (C).","tr":"\"Nedenini sormaya ve anlayabileceği bir cevap almaya hakkı var\": explanation (C).","fa":"«حق دارد بپرسد چرا و جوابی بگیرد که بفهمد»: explanation (C)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"In practice, officials have rarely ___ a program’s recommendation.","correct":1,"evidence":"staff very rarely challenge the program's recommendation","why":{"en":"\"Very rarely challenge\": challenged (B), a past participle after \"have\".","tr":"\"Çok nadiren itiraz ediyor\": challenged (B), \"have\"den sonra geçmiş ortaç.","fa":"«خیلی به‌ندرت زیر سؤال می‌برند»: challenged (B)، اسم مفعول بعد از «have»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"When something goes wrong, it is often unclear who is ___.","correct":6,"evidence":"it becomes unclear who is responsible","why":{"en":"\"It becomes unclear who is responsible\": responsible (G).","tr":"\"Kimin sorumlu olduğu belirsizleşiyor\": responsible (G).","fa":"«معلوم نیست چه کسی مسئول است»: responsible (G)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"Because testing and human review also cost money, the savings may be ___ than expected.","correct":7,"evidence":"the savings may turn out to be smaller than promised","why":{"en":"\"Smaller than promised\" = smaller than expected (H).","tr":"\"Vaat edilenden küçük\" = beklenenden küçük (H).","fa":"«کمتر از آنچه وعده داده شده» یعنی کمتر از انتظار (H)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 36-39. Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-39 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","qtype":"ynng","questions":[{"n":36,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Computer programs can be valuable for routine public tasks.","correct":"YES","evidence":"a well-designed program can be extremely useful","why":{"en":"Where a task is routine, \"a well-designed program can be extremely useful\".","tr":"Görev rutin olduğunda \"iyi tasarlanmış bir program son derece yararlı olabilir\".","fa":"وقتی کار روزمره است، «یک برنامه‌ی خوب طراحی‌شده می‌تواند خیلی مفید باشد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"An explanation produced after a decision is as good as the original reason.","correct":"NO","evidence":"An explanation that is constructed after the event is a story about a decision","why":{"en":"Researchers suggest it; the writer is \"not convinced\": it is \"a story about a decision, not the reason\".","tr":"Araştırmacılar bunu öneriyor; yazar \"ikna olmadı\": bu \"kararla ilgili bir hikâye, nedeni değil\".","fa":"پژوهشگرها این را پیشنهاد می‌کنند؛ نویسنده «قانع نشده»: این «داستانی درباره‌ی تصمیم است، نه دلیلش»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":38,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Most public bodies already tell people what data their programs use.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"the public should be told what data they use","why":{"en":"The writer says the public \"should be told\". Nothing is said about what most public bodies do now.","tr":"Yazar halkın \"bilgilendirilmesi gerektiğini\" söylüyor. Kamu kurumlarının çoğunun şu an ne yaptığına dair bir şey yok.","fa":"نویسنده می‌گوید مردم «باید مطلع شوند». درباره‌ی کاری که بیشتر نهادها الان می‌کنند چیزی نیامده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":39,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Banning these programs would be the best way to deal with their problems.","correct":"NO","evidence":"the answer is not to ban these tools","why":{"en":"\"The answer is not to ban these tools, nor to trust them blindly. It is to limit what they are used for.\"","tr":"\"Çözüm bu araçları yasaklamak ya da onlara körü körüne güvenmek değil. Ne için kullanıldıklarını sınırlamak.\"","fa":"«راه‌حل نه ممنوع کردن این ابزارهاست و نه اعتماد کورکورانه به آن‌ها. باید محدود کرد برای چه به کار می‌روند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]}]},{"instruction":"Question 40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in box 40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which of the following is the most suitable title for Reading Passage 3?","options":["A How computers will replace public officials","B A short history of computers in government","C Why some public decisions must stay with people","D Saving public money through automation"],"correct":2,"evidence":"which decisions belong to people who can be questioned","why":{"en":"The whole argument ends with \"which decisions belong to people who can be questioned\". The other titles are too narrow or say the opposite.","tr":"Bütün tartışma \"hangi kararların sorgulanabilecek insanlara ait olduğu\" ile bitiyor. Diğer başlıklar ya çok dar ya da tersini söylüyor.","fa":"کل استدلال با «کدام تصمیم‌ها مال آدم‌هایی است که می‌شود از آن‌ها سؤال کرد» تمام می‌شود. عنوان‌های دیگر یا خیلی محدودند یا برعکس را می‌گویند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The writer is not convinced by this claim.\" This means the writer...","options":["doubts it","agrees with it","has not read it"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Not convinced = not persuaded, so the writer doubts it.","tr":"Not convinced = ikna olmamış; yazar ondan şüphe ediyor.","fa":"not convinced یعنی قانع نشده، پس نویسنده به آن شک دارد."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"goes against a program’s advice\"?","options":["follows its score","updates its records","challenges its recommendation"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"To challenge a recommendation = to question it and not simply accept it.","tr":"Bir öneriye challenge etmek = onu sorgulamak, olduğu gibi kabul etmemek.","fa":"challenge کردنِ یک توصیه یعنی زیر سؤال بردنش و قبول نکردنِ ساده‌اش."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"When is the best time to answer a question about the best title for a passage?","options":["before reading the passage","after the other questions","straight after the first paragraph"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"By then you know the whole argument, and the title must cover all of it.","tr":"O zamana kadar bütün düşünce çizgisini bilirsin; başlık da hepsini kapsamalı.","fa":"تا آن موقع کل استدلال را می‌دانی و عنوان باید همه‌اش را پوشش بدهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Supporters say the system saves money. I think the savings are exaggerated.\" Statement: \"The system saves a great deal of money.\" YES, NO or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NO","YES","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The claim is the supporters’. The writer thinks the savings are exaggerated: NO.","tr":"İddia destekçilere ait. Yazar tasarrufların abartıldığını düşünüyor: NO.","fa":"ادعا مال طرفداران است. نویسنده فکر می‌کند صرفه‌جویی اغراق شده: NO."}},{"tests":"trap","point":2,"prompt":"Summary gap: \"officials have rarely ___ the advice\". Which word from a box fits the grammar?","options":["question","questions","questioned"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"After \"have\", the verb must be a past participle: questioned.","tr":"\"Have\"den sonra fiil geçmiş ortaç olmalı: questioned.","fa":"بعد از «have» فعل باید اسم مفعول باشد: questioned."}}],"id":"c-x02-r3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 3: a long article","tr":"GT Reading Section 3: uzun bir makale","fa":"GT Reading Section 3: یک مقاله‌ی بلند"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to choose a heading for each section of a long article, complete a short summary with single words, and answer multiple-choice questions about details.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir makalenin her bölümü için bir başlık seçmeyi, kısa bir özeti tek kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve ayrıntılarla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری برای هر بخش یک مقاله‌ی بلند عنوان انتخاب کنی، یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه را با تک‌کلمه‌ها کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی جزئیات جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-F"},{"label":{"en":"Headings","tr":"Başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌ها"},"value":"i-ix"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: help at the nest","tr":"Bu sınav: yuvada yardım","fa":"این آزمون: کمک در لانه"},"intro":{"en":"Section 3 is one long article on a general subject: nature, history or daily life. It is the longest GT text, so headings help you build a map of it before you look for details.","tr":"Section 3 genel bir konuda tek bir uzun makaledir: doğa, tarih ya da günlük hayat. GT’nin en uzun metnidir; bu yüzden başlıklar, ayrıntılara bakmadan önce metnin bir haritasını çıkarmana yardım eder.","fa":"Section 3 یک مقاله‌ی بلند درباره‌ی یک موضوع عمومی است: طبیعت، تاریخ یا زندگی روزمره. طولانی‌ترین متن GT است، پس عنوان‌ها کمکت می‌کنند قبل از گشتن دنبال جزئیات، نقشه‌ی متن را بسازی."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r3gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT3-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-nature","n":12,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 12 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 12’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۲ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Birds that help at the nest","tr":"Yuvada yardım eden kuşlar","fa":"پرنده‌هایی که در لانه کمک می‌کنند"},"asks":{"en":"Section 3 is one long article for a general reader. Here it explains why some birds raise their young with extra helpers: who the helpers are, what they do, why they help and where it happens.","tr":"Section 3 genel okur için yazılmış uzun bir makaledir. Burada bazı kuşların yavrularını neden ek yardımcılarla büyüttüğü anlatılıyor: yardımcıların kim olduğu, ne yaptıkları, neden yardım ettikleri ve bunun nerede görüldüğü.","fa":"Section 3 یک مقاله‌ی بلند برای خواننده‌ی عمومی است. این‌جا توضیح می‌دهد چرا بعضی پرنده‌ها جوجه‌هایشان را با کمک‌کننده‌های اضافه بزرگ می‌کنند: کمک‌کننده‌ها چه کسانی‌اند، چه می‌کنند، چرا کمک می‌کنند و کجا این اتفاق می‌افتد."},"fields":["A puzzle","Who helps","What helpers do","Why they help","Where it happens","Groups that need helpers"],"words":[{"a":"raise young","b":"bring up chicks","tr":"yavru büyütmek","fa":"بزرگ کردن جوجه‌ها"},{"a":"territory","b":"the area a bird defends","tr":"bölge","fa":"قلمرو"},{"a":"inherit","b":"get something when the owner dies or leaves","tr":"miras almak","fa":"به ارث بردن"},{"a":"predator","b":"an animal that hunts others","tr":"yırtıcı","fa":"شکارچی"},{"a":"survive to adulthood","b":"live until they are adults","tr":"yetişkinliğe kadar yaşamak","fa":"تا بزرگسالی زنده ماندن"},{"a":"relatives","b":"family members / brothers and sisters","tr":"akrabalar","fa":"خویشاوندان"},{"a":"unpredictable","b":"changing without warning","tr":"öngörülemez","fa":"غیرقابل‌پیش‌بینی"},{"a":"essential","b":"cannot manage without","tr":"zorunlu, vazgeçilmez","fa":"ضروری"},{"a":"compete for","b":"try to get before others do","tr":"... için rekabet etmek","fa":"برای ... رقابت کردن"},{"a":"insurance against","b":"protection from","tr":"... karşı güvence","fa":"بیمه در برابرِ"}],"traps":[{"en":"A heading that repeats a word from the section is not always right. Choose the heading that sums up the whole section, not one sentence.","tr":"Bölümden bir kelimeyi tekrar eden başlık her zaman doğru değildir. Tek bir cümleyi değil, bütün bölümü özetleyen başlığı seç.","fa":"عنوانی که کلمه‌ای از بخش را تکرار می‌کند همیشه درست نیست. عنوانی را انتخاب کن که کل بخش را خلاصه می‌کند، نه یک جمله را."},{"en":"MCQ options often take true details from the wrong place. Find the sentence the question is about before you compare the options.","tr":"Çoktan seçmeli seçenekler çoğu zaman doğru ayrıntıları yanlış yerden alır. Seçenekleri karşılaştırmadan önce sorunun ilgili olduğu cümleyi bul.","fa":"گزینه‌های چندگزینه‌ای اغلب جزئیاتِ درست را از جای غلط برمی‌دارند. قبل از مقایسه‌ی گزینه‌ها، جمله‌ای را که سؤال درباره‌اش است پیدا کن."}],"example":{"text":"\"C  Some seabirds fly thousands of kilometres to feed, yet they return to the same nest every year. Scientists think they use the sun, smells and even the Earth’s magnetism to find their way.\"","item":"Best heading for C: i How seabirds find food  ii How seabirds navigate home  iii The dangers of long flights","answer":"ii","why":{"en":"Food is mentioned, but the section is about how they find their way back.","tr":"Yiyecekten söz ediliyor ama bölüm geri dönüş yolunu nasıl bulduklarıyla ilgili.","fa":"از غذا اسم برده شده، اما بخش درباره‌ی این است که راه برگشت را چطور پیدا می‌کنند."}}},{"id":"GT3-nature","ctx":["GT3-nature"],"title":{"en":"Nature and the environment","tr":"Doğa ve çevre","fa":"طبیعت و محیط زیست"},"asks":{"en":"A longer text about wildlife or the environment: turtles, storks, farmland returning to nature, plastic in the sea. Multiple choice, summaries and matching features test causes, efforts and results.","tr":"Yaban hayatı ya da çevre hakkında daha uzun bir metin: kaplumbağalar, leylekler, doğaya dönen tarım arazileri, denizdeki plastik. Çoktan seçmeli sorular, özetler ve özellik eşleştirme nedenleri, çabaları ve sonuçları sınar.","fa":"متنی بلندتر درباره‌ی حیات وحش یا محیط زیست: لاک‌پشت‌ها، لک‌لک‌ها، زمین‌های کشاورزی که به طبیعت برمی‌گردند، پلاستیک در دریا. چندگزینه‌ای، خلاصه‌ها و جورکردن ویژگی‌ها علت‌ها، تلاش‌ها و نتیجه‌ها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Why did the birds disappear from the area?","What did volunteers do first?","Summary: the young turtles head for the ___.","Which organisation does each statement refer to?"],"words":[{"a":"wildlife","b":"animals and birds","tr":"yaban hayatı","fa":"حیات وحش"},{"a":"habitat","b":"the place where it lives","tr":"yaşam alanı","fa":"زیستگاه"},{"a":"return","b":"come back / reappear","tr":"geri dönmek","fa":"برگشتن"},{"a":"breed","b":"have young / nest","tr":"üremek","fa":"تولیدمثل کردن"},{"a":"pollution","b":"dirty water or air / waste","tr":"kirlilik","fa":"آلودگی"},{"a":"volunteers","b":"unpaid helpers","tr":"gönüllüler","fa":"داوطلب‌ها"},{"a":"monitor","b":"watch and record","tr":"izlemek","fa":"پایش کردن"},{"a":"release","b":"set free","tr":"serbest bırakmak","fa":"رها کردن"},{"a":"population","b":"the number of animals","tr":"popülasyon","fa":"جمعیت"},{"a":"threatened","b":"in danger","tr":"tehdit altında","fa":"در معرض خطر"},{"a":"reintroduce","b":"bring back to an area","tr":"yeniden yerleştirmek","fa":"بازگرداندن به منطقه"},{"a":"rewilding","b":"letting land return to nature","tr":"doğaya geri bırakma","fa":"بازگرداندن زمین به طبیعت"}],"traps":[{"en":"Cause and result in one paragraph: the question may ask for the cause, but the result comes first in the text.","tr":"Neden ve sonuç aynı paragrafta: soru nedeni sorabilir ama metinde önce sonuç gelir.","fa":"علت و نتیجه در یک پاراگراف: سؤال ممکن است علت را بخواهد، ولی در متن اول نتیجه می‌آید."},{"en":"Summary from a box: two words in the box are close in meaning. Check the exact sense.","tr":"Kutudan özet: kutudaki iki kelime anlamca yakındır. Tam anlamı kontrol et.","fa":"خلاصه از جعبه: دو کلمه‌ی جعبه معنی نزدیکی دارند. معنی دقیق را چک کن."}],"example":{"text":"Storks stopped nesting in the region in the 1940s, after the wet meadows where they fed were drained for farming. They returned only when some of the meadows were flooded again in 2016.","item":"Why did storks stop nesting in the region?  A hunting   B the loss of wet meadows   C cold winters","answer":"B","why":{"en":"\"After the wet meadows where they fed were drained\": the cause is the loss of their feeding grounds.","tr":"\"Beslendikleri ıslak çayırlar kurutulduktan sonra\": neden, beslenme alanlarının yok olması.","fa":"«بعد از اینکه چمنزارهای خیسی که در آن غذا می‌خوردند زهکشی شدند»: علت از بین رفتن محل تغذیه است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT3-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-nature","n":12,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 12 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 12’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۲ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Headings, a summary, then details","tr":"Başlıklar, bir özet, sonra ayrıntılar","fa":"عنوان‌ها، یک خلاصه، بعد جزئیات"},"body":{"en":"Questions 28-33: choose a heading, i-ix, for each section A-F; three headings are not used. Questions 34-36: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY. Questions 37-40: multiple choice, A-D.","tr":"Soru 28-33: her bölüm (A-F) için i-ix arasından bir başlık seç; üç başlık kullanılmaz. Soru 34-36: özeti ONE WORD ONLY ile tamamla. Soru 37-40: çoktan seçmeli, A-D.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۸ تا ۳۳: برای هر بخش (A تا F) یک عنوان از i تا ix انتخاب کن؛ سه عنوان استفاده نمی‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۳۴ تا ۳۶: خلاصه را با ONE WORD ONLY کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۳۷ تا ۴۰: چندگزینه‌ای، A تا D."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Read for the job of each section","tr":"Her bölümün görevini bulmak için oku","fa":"برای پیدا کردن کارِ هر بخش بخوان"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the headings and notice how they differ: a cause, a place, a problem, an example.","tr":"Başlıkları oku ve nasıl farklılaştıklarına dikkat et: bir neden, bir yer, bir sorun, bir örnek.","fa":"عنوان‌ها را بخوان و ببین چه فرقی دارند: یک دلیل، یک مکان، یک مشکل، یک مثال."},{"en":"Read each section and say its job in three or four words of your own.","tr":"Her bölümü oku ve görevini kendi kelimelerinle üç dört kelimeyle söyle.","fa":"هر بخش را بخوان و کارش را با سه چهار کلمه از خودت بگو."},{"en":"Choose the heading that fits the whole section. Cross it out, so you do not use it twice.","tr":"Bütün bölüme uyan başlığı seç. İki kez kullanmamak için üstünü çiz.","fa":"عنوانی را انتخاب کن که به کل بخش می‌خورد. خطش بزن تا دو بار استفاده‌اش نکنی."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Same word, wrong heading","tr":"Aynı kelime, yanlış başlık","fa":"کلمه‌ی یکسان، عنوان غلط"},"body":{"en":"A heading may contain a word that appears in the section, such as \"calls\" or \"food\", and still be wrong. Headings are about the main idea, so check the first and last sentences of the section as well as the details.","tr":"Bir başlık bölümde geçen bir kelimeyi, örneğin \"calls\" ya da \"food\", içerebilir ve yine de yanlış olabilir. Başlıklar ana fikirle ilgilidir; ayrıntıların yanında bölümün ilk ve son cümlelerine de bak.","fa":"یک عنوان ممکن است کلمه‌ای را که در بخش آمده، مثل «calls» یا «food»، داشته باشد و باز هم غلط باشد. عنوان‌ها درباره‌ی ایده‌ی اصلی‌اند، پس علاوه بر جزئیات، جمله‌ی اول و آخر بخش را هم چک کن."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One heading, step by step","tr":"Bir başlık, adım adım","fa":"یک عنوان، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Choose the correct heading for the section.","text":"\"D  Squirrels bury thousands of nuts each autumn. Many are never found again, and some grow into trees. In this way, the animals help forests to spread.\"","item":"i How squirrels find buried nuts  ii An unplanned benefit to forests  iii Why squirrels prefer nuts","answer":"ii","walk":[{"en":"Say the job of the section: forgotten nuts grow into trees.","tr":"Bölümün görevini söyle: unutulan fındıklar ağaca dönüşüyor.","fa":"کار بخش را بگو: فندق‌های فراموش‌شده درخت می‌شوند."},{"en":"Heading i uses \"buried nuts\", but the section says many are never found.","tr":"i başlığı \"buried nuts\" kullanıyor ama bölüm çoğunun hiç bulunmadığını söylüyor.","fa":"عنوان i «buried nuts» را دارد، اما بخش می‌گوید خیلی‌هایشان هیچ‌وقت پیدا نمی‌شوند."},{"en":"The last sentence gives the main idea: the forest benefits. Choose ii.","tr":"Son cümle ana fikri veriyor: orman fayda görüyor. ii’yi seç.","fa":"جمله‌ی آخر ایده‌ی اصلی را می‌دهد: جنگل سود می‌برد. ii را انتخاب کن."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"A section describes three dangers to young turtles and ends: \"Only one in a thousand reaches adulthood.\" Which heading fits best?","options":["Where turtles lay their eggs","How long turtles live","A difficult start in life"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The dangers and the \"one in a thousand\" ending are about how hard early life is.","tr":"Tehlikeler ve \"binde bir\" sonu, yaşamın başlangıcının ne kadar zor olduğuyla ilgili.","fa":"خطرها و پایانِ «یکی از هزار» درباره‌ی این است که شروع زندگی چقدر سخت است."}},"remember":{"en":"Name the job of each section in your own words, then match the heading to the whole section.","tr":"Her bölümün görevini kendi kelimelerinle adlandır, sonra başlığı bütün bölümle eşleştir.","fa":"کار هر بخش را با کلمه‌های خودت نام‌گذاری کن و بعد عنوان را با کل بخش جور کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r3-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 3","title":{"en":"Help at the nest","tr":"Yuvada yardım","fa":"کمک در لانه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT3-nature"],"texts":[{"title":"Help at the nest","kind":"article","body":"A  Most birds raise their young in pairs: a male and a female build a nest, keep the eggs warm and bring food to the chicks until they can look after themselves. In roughly one species in ten, however, ornithologists have found something different. At these nests, the parents are joined by extra adults that feed and protect chicks which are not their own. These extra birds are known as helpers, and for a long time their behaviour was one of the great puzzles of bird biology. Early naturalists noticed the extra birds but assumed they were simply neighbours passing by. It was only when researchers began to mark individual birds with coloured rings, and to follow the same families for many years, that the true pattern became clear.\n\nB  In most of these species, the helpers are young birds that have stayed with their parents after growing up. The Florida scrub-jay, which lives in the dry oak scrub of the south-eastern United States, is a well-studied example. Young scrub-jays often remain at home for a year or two. They do not stay because they are too young to breed; rather, every suitable piece of land nearby is already occupied, and a bird without a territory cannot raise a family. By waiting at home, a young jay stays safe and well fed, and it may eventually inherit part of its parents' land. Some young males even expand the family territory and later take over a corner of it for themselves.\n\nC  The work that helpers do is very similar to that of the parents. They bring insects to the nest, remove waste and keep watch for danger. When a snake or a hawk comes near, the whole group may attack it together, a behaviour known as mobbing, which a pair on its own would be much less able to manage. In many species, nests with helpers produce more young that survive to adulthood, and parents with helpers also tend to live longer, because the hard work of feeding the chicks is shared. In the superb fairy-wren of Australia, for example, females with several helpers can afford to lay slightly smaller eggs, since they know that plenty of food will arrive once the chicks hatch.\n\nD  The great question is why a bird should spend its energy on chicks that are not its own. The main answer is family. Because helpers are usually feeding their younger brothers and sisters, they are helping to pass on genes that they share. Long-tailed tits in Britain show this particularly clearly. Their nests are often destroyed, usually by a predator such as a magpie, and once the season is too far advanced to start again, the unlucky pair will often go to help at the nest of a brother. Remarkably, they seem able to tell relatives from other birds by their calls, which each bird learns from its parents while it is still in the nest.\n\nE  Helping is not spread evenly around the world. It is far more common in Australia and in parts of Africa than in Europe or North America. Researchers who compared thousands of species found that group breeding is most common where rainfall, and therefore the food supply, changes greatly and unpredictably from year to year. In a good year a group can raise many chicks; in a bad year, the extra adults may make the difference between some chicks surviving and none at all. A pair living alone in the same conditions would often fail completely, and in a long dry period it might not breed for several years. Living in a group, it seems, is a kind of insurance against hard times.\n\nF  For some species, helpers are not just useful but essential. The white-winged chough of eastern Australia feeds its young on insects dug from the ground, a slow and difficult task, and a breeding group usually needs at least four adults to raise any chicks at all. Groups compete fiercely for young birds, and there are even reports of groups luring young birds away from neighbouring groups to increase their own numbers. Scientists still disagree about many details, including why helping is so rare in some families of birds and so common in others, and new behaviours are reported every year. What is clear is that the simple picture of two parents and a nest tells only part of the story of how birds raise their young. For a surprising number of species, raising a family is a job for the whole household."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 28-33. The text has six sections, A-F. Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. Write the correct number, i-ix, in boxes 28-33 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"headings","bank":["i Why most birds raise their young in pairs","ii Passing on shared genes by helping the family","iii Species that cannot breed in small groups","iv Extra adults at the nest","v A link with unpredictable weather","vi Sharing the daily tasks of parenthood","vii Young birds waiting for land of their own","viii Learning calls from parents","ix Why helping birds are becoming rarer"],"questions":[{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section A","correct":3,"evidence":"the parents are joined by extra adults","why":{"en":"A introduces the extra adults that feed chicks which are not their own: iv. Heading i repeats \"in pairs\", but that is only the opening.","tr":"A, kendi yavruları olmayan civcivleri besleyen ek yetişkinleri tanıtıyor: iv. i başlığı \"in pairs\"i tekrar ediyor ama bu yalnızca giriş.","fa":"A بزرگسال‌های اضافه‌ای را معرفی می‌کند که به جوجه‌هایی غذا می‌دهند که مال خودشان نیست: iv. عنوان i «in pairs» را تکرار می‌کند، اما این فقط شروع بخش است."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section B","correct":6,"evidence":"every suitable piece of land nearby is already occupied","why":{"en":"Young jays stay at home because all the land is taken, and may later inherit some: vii.","tr":"Genç alakargalar bütün arazi dolu olduğu için evde kalıyor ve sonra bir kısmını miras alabiliyor: vii.","fa":"زاغ‌های جوان خانه می‌مانند چون همه‌ی زمین‌ها گرفته شده و شاید بعداً بخشی را به ارث ببرند: vii."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section C","correct":5,"evidence":"The work that helpers do is very similar to that of the parents","why":{"en":"Feeding, cleaning, keeping watch and mobbing predators: helpers share the parents’ daily tasks, vi.","tr":"Beslemek, temizlemek, gözcülük etmek ve yırtıcılara toplu saldırmak: yardımcılar ebeveynlerin günlük işlerini paylaşıyor, vi.","fa":"غذا دادن، تمیز کردن، نگهبانی و حمله‌ی گروهی به شکارچی: کمک‌کننده‌ها کارهای روزانه‌ی پدر و مادر را با آن‌ها تقسیم می‌کنند، vi."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section D","correct":1,"evidence":"they are helping to pass on genes that they share","why":{"en":"Helpers feed relatives and so pass on shared genes: ii. Calls are only one detail, so viii is wrong.","tr":"Yardımcılar akrabalarını besliyor ve böylece ortak genleri aktarıyor: ii. Sesler yalnızca bir ayrıntı; viii yanlış.","fa":"کمک‌کننده‌ها به خویشاوندانشان غذا می‌دهند و ژن‌های مشترک را منتقل می‌کنند: ii. صداها فقط یک جزئیات‌اند، پس viii غلط است."},"trap":["TR-samewords","TR-detail"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section E","correct":4,"evidence":"changes greatly and unpredictably from year to year","why":{"en":"Group breeding is most common where rainfall changes \"unpredictably from year to year\": v.","tr":"Grupla üreme, yağışın \"yıldan yıla öngörülemez biçimde\" değiştiği yerlerde en yaygın: v.","fa":"زادآوری گروهی جایی رایج‌تر است که بارش «از سالی به سال دیگر به‌طور غیرقابل‌پیش‌بینی» تغییر می‌کند: v."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","PARA-cause"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"Section F","correct":2,"evidence":"helpers are not just useful but essential","why":{"en":"Choughs need at least four adults to raise any chicks: iii.","tr":"Beyaz kanatlı dağ kargaları herhangi bir yavru büyütmek için en az dört yetişkine ihtiyaç duyuyor: iii.","fa":"کلاغ‌های بال‌سفید برای بزرگ کردن حتی یک جوجه دست‌کم چهار بزرگسال لازم دارند: iii."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 34-36. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 34-36 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"Long-tailed tits","questions":[{"n":34,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Long-tailed tit nests are often destroyed, in most cases by a ___.","accept":["predator"],"limit":1,"evidence":"usually by a predator such as a magpie","why":{"en":"\"Usually by a predator such as a magpie\": in most cases = usually.","tr":"\"Genellikle saksağan gibi bir yırtıcı tarafından\": in most cases = usually.","fa":"«معمولاً به دست یک شکارچی مثل زاغی»: in most cases یعنی usually."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-limit"]},{"n":35,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Late in the season, the pair will often help at the nest of a ___.","accept":["brother"],"limit":1,"evidence":"go to help at the nest of a brother","why":{"en":"\"The unlucky pair will often go to help at the nest of a brother.\"","tr":"\"Şanssız çift çoğu zaman bir erkek kardeşin yuvasına yardıma gider.\"","fa":"«جفتِ بدشانس اغلب برای کمک به لانه‌ی یک برادر می‌رود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"They appear to recognise their relatives by their ___.","accept":["calls"],"limit":1,"evidence":"by their calls, which each bird learns from its parents","why":{"en":"\"They seem able to tell relatives from other birds by their calls.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Akrabalarını diğer kuşlardan seslerinden ayırt edebiliyor gibiler.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«به نظر می‌رسد خویشاوندان را از روی صدایشان از پرنده‌های دیگر تشخیص می‌دهند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 37-40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":37,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about some young male scrub-jays?","options":["A They leave home before their first winter.","B They make their parents’ area bigger and later claim a section of it.","C They help at the nests of neighbouring pairs.","D They are driven away by their parents."],"correct":1,"evidence":"Some young males even expand the family territory and later take over a corner of it","why":{"en":"\"Some young males even expand the family territory and later take over a corner of it for themselves.\" Nothing says they leave early, help neighbours or are driven away.","tr":"\"Bazı genç erkekler aile bölgesini genişletiyor ve sonra bir köşesini kendilerine alıyor.\" Erken ayrıldıkları, komşulara yardım ettikleri ya da kovuldukları söylenmiyor.","fa":"«بعضی نرهای جوان حتی قلمرو خانواده را بزرگ‌تر می‌کنند و بعد گوشه‌ای از آن را برای خودشان برمی‌دارند.» هیچ‌جا نگفته زود از خانه می‌روند، به همسایه‌ها کمک می‌کنند یا پدر و مادر بیرونشان می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-detail","PARA-cause"]},{"n":38,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"According to the writer, nests with helpers","options":["A are built more quickly.","B are attacked less often by snakes.","C raise a larger number of chicks to maturity.","D contain more eggs."],"correct":2,"evidence":"nests with helpers produce more young that survive to adulthood","why":{"en":"\"Nests with helpers produce more young that survive to adulthood.\" Fairy-wrens with helpers lay smaller eggs, not more.","tr":"\"Yardımcılı yuvalar yetişkinliğe kadar yaşayan daha çok yavru çıkarıyor.\" Yardımcısı olan dişi fairy-wren’ler daha çok değil, daha küçük yumurta yumurtluyor.","fa":"«لانه‌های دارای کمک‌کننده جوجه‌های بیشتری تا بزرگسالی بار می‌آورند». ماده‌های fairy-wren که کمک‌کننده دارند تخم کوچک‌تر می‌گذارند، نه بیشتر."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":39,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Group breeding is common in parts of Africa and Australia because","options":["A there are fewer predators there.","B birds there live longer.","C there is more space for territories.","D the amount of food available varies widely between years."],"correct":3,"evidence":"where rainfall, and therefore the food supply, changes greatly","why":{"en":"It is most common \"where rainfall, and therefore the food supply, changes greatly and unpredictably\".","tr":"En çok \"yağışın ve dolayısıyla besin kaynağının büyük ölçüde değiştiği\" yerlerde görülüyor.","fa":"بیشتر جایی دیده می‌شود که «بارش و در نتیجه غذا خیلی تغییر می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","PARA-cause"]},{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about white-winged choughs?","options":["A A breeding group must include a minimum of four adults.","B They feed their young mainly on fruit.","C They avoid contact with other groups.","D They breed only in years with good rain."],"correct":0,"evidence":"a breeding group usually needs at least four adults","why":{"en":"\"A breeding group usually needs at least four adults to raise any chicks at all.\" They feed on insects and compete with other groups.","tr":"\"Bir üreme grubunun herhangi bir yavru büyütebilmesi için genelde en az dört yetişkin gerekir.\" Böceklerle besleniyorlar ve diğer gruplarla rekabet ediyorlar.","fa":"«یک گروه معمولاً دست‌کم چهار بزرگسال لازم دارد تا اصلاً جوجه‌ای بزرگ کند». با حشره تغذیه می‌کنند و با گروه‌های دیگر رقابت دارند."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r3-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The birds mob any hawk that comes near.\" To mob a hawk means to...","options":["run away from it","attack it together","follow it quietly"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Mobbing = a group attacking a predator together to drive it away.","tr":"Mobbing = bir grubun bir yırtıcıyı kovmak için birlikte saldırması.","fa":"mobbing یعنی حمله‌ی گروهی به یک شکارچی برای فراری دادنش."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A heading says \"A link with the seasons\". Which sentence would match it?","options":["Most frogs in the area lay their eggs only when the spring rains begin.","The frogs are green with brown spots.","Scientists counted the frogs for ten years."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Eggs laid only when the spring rains begin = breeding linked to a season.","tr":"Yumurtaların yalnızca bahar yağmurları başlayınca bırakılması = üremenin bir mevsime bağlı olması.","fa":"تخم‌گذاری فقط وقتی باران‌های بهاری شروع می‌شود = تولیدمثلی که به یک فصل وابسته است."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"You chose heading v for section B, but section E seems to fit v as well. What do you do?","options":["Use v for both sections","Leave section E empty","Compare both: each heading is used only once"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Each heading fits only one section. Decide which section v sums up best.","tr":"Her başlık yalnızca bir bölüme uyar. v’nin hangi bölümü en iyi özetlediğine karar ver.","fa":"هر عنوان فقط به یک بخش می‌خورد. تصمیم بگیر v کدام بخش را بهتر خلاصه می‌کند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"A section is about how bees find flowers; one sentence mentions the colour of the hive. A heading says \"The colour of the hive\". Is it the right heading?","options":["Yes: the same words appear in the section","No: it matches one detail, not the main idea","Yes, if it is the first heading in the list"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Headings sum up the whole section. A shared word in one sentence is a trap.","tr":"Başlıklar bütün bölümü özetler. Tek bir cümledeki ortak kelime bir tuzaktır.","fa":"عنوان‌ها کل بخش را خلاصه می‌کنند. کلمه‌ی مشترک در یک جمله یک دام است."}}],"id":"c-x02-r3-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r3"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
